{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The land of the children of his people</b> — of Balak; he was from there, and he would prophesy and say to him: 'You are destined to reign.' This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 22:5), from aggadic teachings (Numbers Rabbah 20:7). But its plain sense is: 'the land of the children of his people' — of Balaam, for there he was born and there is his family origin. And the reason for mentioning this is because he was a soothsayer from a land whose entire people practice soothsaying, as it is written: 'For they are full from the east and soothsayers like the Philistines' (Isaiah 2:6)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:38.188408917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}